      "writtenOn": "2025-02-12T18:19:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Atomic adds extra overhead, but here I want to specifically cause contention, and I am concerned that AtomicReference could make the tests avoid concurrency and pass when they might otherwise fail. However, I discovered here https://stackoverflow.com/questions/8344509/equivalent-of-atomicreference-but-without-the-volatile-synchronization-cost the getPlain() and setPlain() methods which make this finally what java needed. Done.",
